# ws/os-scm — replace the /proc columnar handoff with SCM_RIGHTS

#
# Change: the bulk-loaded columnar store keeps its sealed memfd, its exact
# FPCOLUMN payload and its "FPQCOL1 <pid> <fd> <bytes> <rows>" descriptor, but
# the descriptor itself is now delivered over an AF_UNIX SOCK_SEQPACKET control
# socket with SCM_RIGHTS.  The client publishes a per-load abstract address
# ("@fpqcol-<pid>-<n>"), the new three-argument load function connects and sends
# one record (magic, backend pid, bytes, rows) with the memfd attached, and the
# client validates SO_PEERCRED against PQbackendPID before mapping it.  The
# client never opens /proc/<pid>/fd/<fd>, so it no longer needs the backend's
# UID or ptrace-read permission.  The two-argument function is unchanged and
# still returns the original /proc descriptor; the client falls back to it for
# an older server or a failed transfer.
#
# The store remains opt-in: only fastpostgres.columnar.load()/the explicit SQL
# function touch it.  The ring, the DB-API default read and the stream()/reduce
# paths are untouched.

