    flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g \
      -v $SCRIPT:/usr/local/bin/columnar_scan.py:ro \
      -e BENCH_GIT_REV=os-scm fpq-os-scm python3 /usr/local/bin/columnar_scan.py 100000'

Three alternating runs per image (baseline, os-scm, baseline, os-scm, baseline,
os-scm); the result lines below are the medians and every per-run value is listed
so the spread travels with the number.  The baseline image has no bulk-load API,
so it prints the heap path and "columnar.path: unavailable".  Page faults are
the client process's own getrusage(RUSAGE_SELF) deltas.

